%I A398712 #49 Oct 20 2026 22:08:56
%S A398712 1,2,3,4,5,8,9,10,13,16,17,29,32,49,53,69,70,77,88,90,92,93,96,149,
%T A398712 170,227,256,276,277,296,320,336,369,469,672,739,753,768,896,904,906,
%U A398712 908,909,936,953,960,964,966,1024,1109,1492,1493,1696,1704,1706,2275
%N A398712 Numbers k such that all of the digits of k are not represented in the Collatz pathway from n to 1.
%C A398712 Is this sequence finite?
%C A398712 a(232) > 10^25 if it exists. - _David A. Corneth_, Sep 11 2026
%C A398712 1 is part of the series because there is no path from 1 to 1 - we have arrived at 1 before any Collatz calculations have taken place.
%H A398712 David A. Corneth and Jeff Sponaugle, <a href="/A398712/b398712.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..231</a> (first 216 terms from David Consiglio)
%H A398712 David A. Corneth, <a href="/A398712/a398712.gp.txt">PARI program</a>
%e A398712 5 is a member of this sequence because 5 --> 16 --> 8 --> 4 --> 2 --> 1 and the digit 5 is not encountered in this pathway (after the initial 5).
%e A398712 29 is in this sequence because 29 --> 88--> 44 --> 22 --> 11 --> 34 --> 17 --> 52 --> 26 --> 13 --> 40 --> 20 --> 10 --> 5 --> 16 --> 8 --> 4 --> 2 --> 1 covers the 2 in 29, but the 9 never appears.
%e A398712 77 is a member because 77 --> 232 --> 116 --> 58 --> 29 --> 88 --> 44 --> 22 --> 11 --> 34 --> 17 --> 52 --> 26 --> 13 --> 40 --> 20 --> 10 --> 5 --> 16 --> 8 --> 4 --> 2 --> 1 has one 7 in it, but both 7s need to appear.
%e A398712 30 is not a member because 30 --> 15 --> 46 --> 23 --> 70 --> ... has both a 3 and a 0.
%o A398712 (Python)
%o A398712 def isok(k):
%o A398712     check = list(str(k))
%o A398712     test = k
%o A398712     while len(check) > 0 and test > 1:
%o A398712         if test % 2 == 0:
%o A398712             test //= 2
%o A398712         else:
%o A398712             test = test * 3 + 1
%o A398712         temp = list(str(test))
%o A398712         for x in temp:
%o A398712             if x in check:
%o A398712                 check.remove(x)
%o A398712     return len(check) != 0
%o A398712 print([k for k in range(1, 3000) if isok(k)])
%o A398712 (PARI) \\ See Corneth link
%K A398712 nonn,base,new
%O A398712 1,2
%A A398712 _David Consiglio, Jr._, Sep 04 2026
